<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Monday 105,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Monday 105,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said Monday's estimate of Iowa and southern Minnesota marketings was 105,000 head, compared with 107,000 a week ago and 104,000 a year ago.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts steady to $0.50 higher than midsession Friday. Trade moderate for light to good demand and light to moderate offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    52.00 -53.50	   53.00 -54.50</p>
<p>few			51.00 -51.50 &amp; 54.00 52.50</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    50.00 -53.50	   50.50 -54.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    46.50 -52.00	   47.00 -53.00</p>
<p>Sows:  mostly steady to 2.00 higher.</p>
<p>US 1-3</p>
<p>300-450 lbs.	   42.50 -45.00	   43.00 -45.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   46.00 -48.00	   46.00 -48.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    48.00 -52.00	   48.00 -53.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass Yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct. lean.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-983-7347--</p>
